#!/bin/bash
# land-gem-studio.sh — "Add to cart" beside every stone, and the page it goes to:
# ring or pendant, the cut, the mount, the metal, the size, and the wallet.
#
# BOTH SIDES (together-city-chat + together-city-react). Vercel AND Railway.
# NO DATABASE MIGRATION.
# PRECONDITION: land-the-stone-has-a-say.sh.
set -euo pipefail

cd "$(dirname "$0")"
[ -d together-city-chat ] || { echo "!! Run this from the Together-Ai repo root."; exit 1; }

if [ -f .git/index.lock ] && [ ! -s .git/index.lock ]; then
  echo "== clearing a stale empty .git/index.lock"
  rm -f .git/index.lock
fi

NEEDS="A gemstone is a commission"
LOG="$(git log --oneline -40)"
case "$LOG" in
  *"$NEEDS"*) echo "== \"$NEEDS\" is already here. Nothing to do."; exit 0 ;;
esac
case "$LOG" in
  *"The stone has a say in its own weight"*) ;;
  *) echo "!! Run land-the-stone-has-a-say.sh first — this is written against the tree it produces."; exit 1 ;;
esac

ALLOWED='^ M together-city-react/(public/assets/img/(apple-touch-icon-180|tc-icon-1024|tc-icon-192|tc-icon-512|tc-icon-maskable-512)\.png|public/downloads/TogetherCity\.apk)$'
DIRTY="$(git status --porcelain \
  | grep -Ev '^\?\? (land-.*\.sh|push-.*\.sh|.*\.patch)$' \
  | grep -Ev "$ALLOWED" || true)"
if [ -n "$DIRTY" ]; then
  echo "!! The tree carries changes this script did not expect:"; echo "$DIRTY"; exit 1
fi

PATCH="$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/land.XXXXXX")"
trap 'rm -f "$PATCH"' EXIT
cat <<'B64EOF' | tr -d '\n' | openssl base64 -d -A > "$PATCH"

B64EOF
WANT="14908af3e261dea908547848a57a14b32154ba5d150be9420f7506c17faae0ff"
GOT="$(shasum -a 256 "$PATCH" | awk '{print $1}')"
[ "$GOT" = "$WANT" ] || { echo "!! Patch is corrupt."; echo "   want $WANT"; echo "   got  $GOT"; exit 1; }
echo "== patch verified"
git apply --check -C1 "$PATCH" || { echo "!! Patch does not apply cleanly. Nothing written."; exit 1; }
git apply -C1 "$PATCH"
echo "== applied"

echo "== gates: the API"
cd together-city-chat
npx tsc --noEmit
npx jest src/astrology
cd ..

echo "== gates: the web app"
cd together-city-react
npx tsc --noEmit
npx vitest run
node scripts/a11y-audit.mjs
node scripts/motion-ceiling.mjs
node scripts/lint-ceiling.mjs
npx vite build
cd ..

git add together-city-chat/src/astrology \
        together-city-react/src/features/astrology \
        together-city-react/src/app/router.tsx \
        together-city-react/src/app/one-stone-answer.test.ts \
        together-city-react/src/styles/layout.css
git commit -F - <<'MSG'
A gemstone is a commission, not a basket item

"Where is the add to cart button next to stones?" — a fair question, and the
answer was that I had over-scoped its blocker. I had it waiting on a database
table for a persistent cart. It never needed one: the button is a NAVIGATION.

Nothing about a gemstone is decided until somebody has said ring or pendant,
which cut, which mount, which metal and what size, and the chart has an opinion
about every one of those. A basket holding "1 x Blue Sapphire" would be a basket
holding nothing anybody could make. So the button beside each stone carries you
into the studio that asks, with that stone, at the weight you are prescribed.

AND BESIDE EVERY CHEAPER ALTERNATIVE TOO. Offering a 1,650 amethyst in place of
a 67,500 sapphire and then only letting somebody buy the sapphire is not
offering an alternative.

THE STUDIO IS THE OWNER'S RING STUDIO, TURNED INTO DATA. Ten cuts and eight
mounts, each with the line drawing it was drawn with — line art rather than
photography, which is the right register for a decision about form; a
photograph of somebody else's ring is a picture of a thing we are not selling.
Four pendant styles for the other route. The Indian size chart, with the
diameter a jeweller measures and the circumference a strip of paper gives you.

THE CHART'S OPINION IS SHOWN AND NEVER ENFORCED, and the judgements are that
file's own, transcribed rather than reinvented: a tension mount will crack a
pearl or a coral, an eternity band has no open back and is fashion wear whatever
the chart says, a three-stone works only alongside the planet's allies, and a
bezel is the recommendation for the stones that want protecting. Every one is
labelled against THIS stone's planet and every one stays choosable. Somebody who
wants the eternity band can have it. They cannot have it without being told.

The weight is fixed because it is the chart's business. The only slider that
moves the price is the grade — where you land between the plainest and the
finest stone of that same weight.

TWO THINGS THE PAGE REFUSES TO DO.

It does not send a price. A gemstone is the dearest thing this city sells and
this page has a slider on it; if the amount travelled in the request body, the
amount would be whatever the request said. The client sends the CHOICES and the
server prices them from the same catalogue and the same weight rule the page was
rendered from. It writes the specification too, so the sentence the jeweller
works from and the sentence the citizen approved are the same sentence.

And it does not invent a making charge. We have the owner's stone prices and no
metalwork prices at all, so the quote is for the stone and the page says so —
gold and making come back from the jeweller against the design, before any work
starts. A total with a guessed number inside it is worse than a total that stops
where the data does.

No migration: the charge is recorded in the Financial hub with the full
specification as its label, so there is a receipt with everything on it. A gem
order of its own — status, the jeweller's quote, a history — needs a table, and
that is the next thing rather than a reason to ship nothing.
MSG

echo "== committed"
cat <<'DONE'

===============================================================
 Landed: A gemstone is a commission, not a basket item
 Both sides — push, then Astrology -> Gemstones -> Add to cart.
===============================================================

DONE
